WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.737
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Thursday, November twenty sixth.

2
00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:13.862
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:14.741
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.741 --> 00:00:30.043
Today: Iran says two tankers hit mines in the Strait of Hormuz, new Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia and a tighter Australian warning for Riyadh's financial district, a Saudi national kidnapped in Niger, a cyber incident at the U.S.

5
00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:33.667
Treasury's financial crimes unit, and Congo's Ebola outbreak passing twelve thousand cases.

6
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.636
We start in the Strait of Hormuz.

7
00:00:35.636 --> 00:00:46.907
Reuters reports Iran's Revolutionary Guards Navy said two oil tankers struck naval mines, exploded and caught fire in the strait yesterday, and Iran warned vessels to coordinate their passage.

8
00:00:46.907 --> 00:00:51.990
Al Jazeera, citing the Guards, says the tankers were near Oman's Khasab port.

9
00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.008
Separately, Al Jazeera reports the U.K.

10
00:00:53.008 --> 00:01:03.599
Maritime Trade Operations center received a report of an explosion from an unknown projectile close to a tanker about fifty nautical miles west of Dubai.

11
00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:05.405
Turning to Saudi Arabia.

12
00:01:05.405 --> 00:01:17.663
Reuters reports Saudi civil defense said eleven people were wounded in a strike on a tower in Riyadh's financial district on Tuesday, November twenty fourth, and the Houthis said they also attacked the Ras Tanura refinery.

13
00:01:17.663 --> 00:01:23.502
Al Jazeera reports the Saudi-led coalition said a Houthi projectile struck Jazan port yesterday.

14
00:01:23.502 --> 00:01:33.851
According to A F P, Saudi forces said air defenses destroyed two ballistic missiles fired toward Riyadh, a cruise missile in the west of the country and a drone near Jeddah's port.

15
00:01:33.851 --> 00:01:38.412
An A F P journalist and residents heard an explosion in Riyadh around midnight.

16
00:01:38.412 --> 00:01:52.588
Australia's Smartraveller updated its Saudi Arabia advice today: it remains at do not travel, and now advises avoiding all travel to the King Abdullah Financial District, with Australians in the area told to consider leaving if safe to do so.

17
00:01:52.588 --> 00:01:54.121
Next, Niger.

18
00:01:54.121 --> 00:02:08.841
Reuters reports, citing two security sources, that militants suspected to be from an Islamic State affiliate active in West Africa kidnapped a Saudi national in Niger over the weekend of November twenty first and twenty second, and are holding the person hostage.

19
00:02:08.841 --> 00:02:09.946
On cyber, The Record reports the U.S.

20
00:02:09.946 --> 00:02:22.462
Treasury's Financial Crimes Enforcement Network, FinCEN, took some systems offline after a cybersecurity incident that resulted in unauthorized access to a limited subset of its systems, according to a notice posted on Tuesday, November twenty fourth.

21
00:02:22.462 --> 00:02:32.495
FinCEN said the F B I and the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency are involved in the investigation.

22
00:02:32.495 --> 00:02:35.153
And an update on Congo's Ebola outbreak.

23
00:02:35.153 --> 00:02:43.565
Reuters reports confirmed cases now exceed twelve thousand, according to government data, as responders struggle to bring the outbreak under control.

24
00:02:43.565 --> 00:02:45.772
Now a few quick notes by region.

25
00:02:45.772 --> 00:02:56.239
In Latin America, Noticias Caracol reports two police officers were killed and four wounded in an armed attack on a patrol in rural Padilla, in Colombia's Cauca department.

26
00:02:56.239 --> 00:03:14.735
In the Middle East, an update on Iraq: the Institute for the Study of War says many Kataib Hezbollah members were reportedly folded into two affiliated Popular Mobilization Forces brigades during the government's entry into Jurf al Sakhr, and that the group moved equipment to western Anbar and western Karbala provinces.

27
00:03:14.735 --> 00:03:26.730
On cyber, The Record reports France's national cybersecurity agency is investigating a suspected ransomware attack on the University Hospital of Guadeloupe that forced doctors to postpone surgeries.

28
00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:37.837
Microsoft Threat Intelligence says several threat actors, including groups it tracks as Salt Typhoon and Onyx Sleet, are abusing ARTEX, an A I powered penetration testing framework, to speed up reconnaissance and credential attacks.

29
00:03:37.837 --> 00:03:46.475
On sanctions, Reuters reports a New York jury convicted Huawei on ten of twelve criminal counts, including sanctions violations.

30
00:03:46.475 --> 00:03:48.520
The company says it will appeal.

31
00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.392
That's today's brief.

32
00:03:50.392 --> 00:03:59.939
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

33
00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:08.130
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

34
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.230
This brief is digitally narrated.

35
00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.168
Questions?

36
00:04:11.168 --> 00:04:14.593
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

37
00:04:14.593 --> 00:04:16.707
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
